<title>POLAND: POLAND TO OFFER PLN 5.85 BLN WORTH OF BONDS IN Q3 97.</title>
<headline>POLAND TO OFFER PLN 5.85 BLN WORTH OF BONDS IN Q3 97.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish finance ministry said on Wednesday it will offer 5.85 billion zloty worth of bonds in the third quarter of 1997, compared with 5.664 billion zlotys in the second quarter.  </p>
<p>The ministry Wednesday announced the following timetable of</p>
<p>bond auctions on the domectic market for the third quarter.</p>
<p>    DATE	 BOND TYPE	BOND SYMBOL   AMOUNT (mln zl)</p>
<p>    Jul  2    fixed 2-yr	  AS1099    total of</p>
<p>		  fixed 5-yr	  OS1002     1,000</p>
<p>    Jul  9  floating 10-yr	DZ0707	 600</p>
<p>    Jul 17    fixed 5-yr	  OS1001	 450</p>
<p>		  assimilated</p>
<p>    Jul 30  floating 3-yr	 TP0800	 300</p>
<p>    Jul 30  index-linked 1-yr   RP0998	 150</p>
<p>    Aug  6    fixed 2-yr	  AS1099    total of</p>
<p>		  fixed 5-yr	  OS1002     1,000</p>
<p>    Aug 20  floating 3-yr	 TP0800	 300</p>
<p>    Aug 21    fixed 5-yr	  OS1001	 450</p>
<p>		   assimilated</p>
<p>    Aug 27  index-linked 1-yr   RP0998	 150</p>
<p>   Sept  3    fixed 2-yr	  AS1099	total of</p>
<p>		  fixed 5-yr	  OS1002	 200 and bonds</p>
<p>							unsold at auction on</p>
<p>							Jun 6, Jul 2, Aug 8</p>
<p>   Sept 10  floating 10-yr	DZ0707	 600</p>
<p>   Sept 17  floating  3-yr	TP0800	 200 and bonds</p>
<p>						     unsold at auction on</p>
<p>						     Jul 30, Aug 20</p>
<p>   Sept 18    fixed 5-yr	  OS1001	 450</p>
<p>		  assimilated</p>
<p>Bonds issued in public offers to individuals:</p>
<p> Jul 24-Aug  6  index-linked 1-yr  IR0998     900</p>
<p>		    subscription</p>
<p> Aug 1-Oct  31 floating 3-yr	TZ0800	300</p>
<p> Sept 2-Nov 28 index-linked 1-yr  IR0998    bonds unsold</p>
<p>							  in subscription</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
